{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Kleins extended their stay over Sunday, and we attended *The Marriage of Figaro* this evening. I sat nearer the stage than last time, which made the detail of the acting quite vivid. Lablache is a true Figaro; his agility matches the character’s wit perfectly. Fodor as Susanna was charming, and Dardanelli gave the Countess a dignity that made her jealousy palpable. Donzelli’s Count was commanding, though perhaps too stern for the lighter moments.\n\nThe music, of course, remains the supreme architecture. Mozart’s harmony resolves all tension into a higher unity, much like the spirit finding its home in the state. It is a delight to see art elevate the soul so effortlessly. I am tired but happy, having enjoyed a fine dinner with the Kleins beforehand. Please give my love to the boys.\n\nYour devoted\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080331,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":190,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1128,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-K6YzwHh7dC2Sbh9bLtAeKoR4yY21NWqU","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":924.556,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9856673773987207,"prompt_per_second":1014.5410337502541,"predicted_n":190,"predicted_ms":4555.296,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.102095238095238,"predicted_per_second":41.49016880571536}}